# Damaged records kept as fixed inputs of tests/t25_fuzz_replay.sh:
#   <file> <view> <state> <function>
# open:  the reader accepts the line and the tool runs into undefined
#        behaviour (signed integer overflow) in <function>; a sanitizer
#        build must report that there.  When the reader refuses the record, the row
#        fails as "no report" and is moved to fixed.
# fixed: no sanitizer report in any build.
# refused: the reader refuses the record, so the input no longer reaches
#        <function>; the defect there is NOT fixed.  slot-owner.rec: its window
#        (0.26 s) is shorter than its header's --interval (1 s).  The same
#        overflow (owner tag, ctv_rows.c owner_block) is kept open through
#        slot-owner-holder.rec, the same record with --interval 0.26;
#        slot-queue.rec reaches another line of owner_block (the queue tag).
# Every .rec here has a row.  Found by tests/fuzz_replay.py, but the last
# three, made by hand: the fuzzer reaches their functions only on a pty.
v-count.rec              scroll  open   rd_V
q-count.rec              wide    open   rd_Q
slot-json.rec            json    open   json_cs_rows
slot-owner.rec           wide    refused owner_block
slot-owner-holder.rec    wide    open   owner_block
slot-queue.rec           wide    open   owner_block
slot-detail-queue.rec    detail  open   print_detail_row
slot-detail-chain.rec    detail  open   print_detail_row
pool-sum.rec             scroll  open   pool_print_groups
ident-none-updated.rec   json    fixed  idents_settle
ident-none-removed.rec   trans   fixed  idents_settle
wait-reason-sum.rec      scroll  open   print_thread_waits
idle-lock-sum.rec        pty:50x140:+++++++q  open  screen_summary
session-sum.rec          pty:50x140:+++++++q  open  print_sessions
